#: ../../../reference/interfaces/network-bind-interface.md:2
msgid "network-bind interface"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../reference/interfaces/network-bind-interface.md:4
msgid ""
"`network-bind` allows operating as a network service, typically enabling a "
"snap to run a server."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../reference/interfaces/network-bind-interface.md:6
msgid "Developer details"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../reference/interfaces/network-bind-interface.md:8
msgid ""
"**{ref}`Auto-connect <explanation-interfaces-interface-auto-connection>`**: "
"yes</br>"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../reference/interfaces/network-bind-interface.md:8
msgid "</br>"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../reference/interfaces/network-bind-interface.md:11
msgid ""
"This interface controls a resource shared by the whole system. Snaps that "
"use it can be installed as parallel instances, but every instance acts on "
"the same system resource and snapd does not coordinate between them. Make "
"sure each instance manages different resources, or run only one instance at "
"a time. For an example of configuring services to avoid port conflicts, see "
"{ref}`Ports <interfaces-parallel-installs-ports>`."
msgstr ""
